er from scratch on node1/node2/node3 (AlmaLinux 9), resolving SELinux and firewalld blockers to get SST working, seeded appdb.orders with committed data, then performed a full cold maintenance-window shutdown of all three nodes followed by a clean cold restart (bootstrap from the highest-seqno node, SST/IST rejoin of the others), confirming all committed writes survived and all three members resumed serving. Finally executed the mandatory one-at-a-time OS reboot protocol on all three nodes, proving changed boot_id and full cluster/quorum/data recovery after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-server-galera, mariadb-backup on node1/node2/node3\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306,4444,4567/tcp+udp,4568 on all three nodes\",\"Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with correct per-node wsrep_node_address/name and fixed wsrep_provider path to /usr/lib64/galera/libgalera_smm.so\",\"Set SELinux boolean daemons_enable_cluster_mode=on persistently on all three nodes to fix a mariadb-backup SST connectto denial\",\"Bootstrapped Galera on node1 via galera_new_cluster, set root password, created sstuser and appuser, created appdb.orders with 3 seed rows\",\"Joined node2 and node3 to the cluster via mariabackup SST; verified wsrep_cluster_size=3 and full data replication on all nodes\",\"Enabled mariadb.service for boot-time start on all three nodes\",\"Inserted an additional pre-maintenance committed row (order-4) and confirmed it replicated to all nodes\",\"Performed the maintenance-window shutdown: stopped mariadb on node3, then node2, then node1 (cluster fully down)\",\"Identified node1 as the highest-seqno node (grastate.dat safe_to_bootstrap:1) and re-bootstrapped it, confirming all 4 rows present\",\"Started node2 and node3, confirmed rejoin and a healthy 3/3 Synced/Primary cluster with all 4 rows present on every node\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all three nodes plus healthy cluster/data proof\",\"Rebooted node1, node2, then node3 one at a time via `reboot`, polling each until reachable again\",\"Verified changed boot_id on each node after its reboot, and verified mariadb auto-started with wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary, and all 4 rows intact after each individual node's restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-member Galera cluster established across node1/node2/node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ecce477f6fe843bd\",\"cmd-c7d28594a8f5438d\",\"cmd-1dea2324d5924acb\",\"cmd-33a1893aac1e4983\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped, node2 and node3 joined via SST; node3 shows wsrep_cluster_size=3, status Primary, all Synced\"},{\"requirement\":\"Application data present before maintenance window\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-033fca093e5245bf\",\"cmd-26042bf107d74422\"],\"summary\":\"appdb.orders created with 3 seed rows on node1; order-4-pre-maintenance inserted just before shutdown\"},{\"requirement\":\"Full cluster shutdown for maintenance window\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-29b6cf34553e469a\",\"cmd-79fc55676db2479b\",\"cmd-ef3cd66ba48a4d4c\"],\"summary\":\"mariadb stopped (inactive) on node3, node2, then node1 in sequence -- entire cluster down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster restart after maintenance with all committed writes intact and all three members serving\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0e83840f552e4ef6\",\"cmd-c5157ed86ed140c7\",\"cmd-951c33b6b86e4d18\",\"cmd-73f1be60b8524e74\",\"cmd-e31e3c5e7e364fc4\",\"cmd-5fe72b1df31a4640\",\"cmd-c5aa40ac88c848c2\",\"cmd-570d8f93f32741ec\",\"cmd-f7ad09ced5bf43df\"],\"summary\":\"node1 re-bootstrapped from highest-seqno grastate (seqno 20, safe_to_bootstrap:1) and showed all 4 rows immediately; node2 and node3 restarted and rejoined; all three nodes independently confirm wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary, and all 4 order rows\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 mandatory OS restart: healthy baseline, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-77239043d4244dab\",\"cmd-c5aa40ac88c848c2\",\"cmd-ab4e046109e941df\",\"cmd-e10b7fae73604f49\",\"cmd-ab8f287346bb425d\",\"cmd-61edba7f1bac4181\"],\"summary\":\"baseline boot_id 31b01b46...; healthy cluster/data proof pre-restart; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during restart; boot_id changed to 95821452...; post-restart cluster_size=3/Synced/Primary with all 4 rows\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 mandatory OS restart: healthy baseline, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-112144321f314702\",\"cmd-570d8f93f32741ec\",\"cmd-d818cd4e95534af7\",\"cmd-330f3682c6804545\",\"cmd-ddbcefea8bb2471c\",\"cmd-43cca241782d4c81\"],\"summary\":\"baseline boot_id e31962a9...; healthy cluster/data proof pre-restart; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during restart; boot_id changed to f8fd3d3f...; post-restart cluster_size=3/Synced/Primary with all 4 rows\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 mandatory OS restart: healthy baseline, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ae11a2dee01a48c1\",\"cmd-f7ad09ced5bf43df\",\"cmd-e5eedea3b3624991\",\"cmd-27630324409240d8\",\"cmd-be74478558cd4e6e\",\"cmd-d3e8ff875dcd4d92\"],\"summary\":\"baseline boot_id 54bd1c3e...; healthy cluster/data proof pre-restart; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during restart; boot_id changed to a0d36261...; post-restart cluster_size=3/Synced/Primary with all 4 rows\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final overall cluster health check after all three node restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c04b5d0429cc41f2\"],\"summary\":\"node1 shows wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, and 4 rows in appdb.orders as final confirmation\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-member MariaDB Galera cluster from scratch on node1/node2/node3 (AlmaLinux 9), resolving SELinux and firewalld blockers to get SST working, seeded appdb.orders with committed data, then performed a full cold maintenance-window shutdown of all three nodes followed by a clean cold restart (bootstrap from the highest-seqno node, SST/IST rejoin of the others), confirming all committed writes survived and all three members resumed serving. Finally executed the mandatory one-at-a-time OS reboot protocol on all three nodes, proving changed boot_id and full cluster/quorum/data recovery after each restart.","actions_performed":["Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-server-galera, mariadb-backup on node1/node2/node3","Opened firewalld ports 3306,4444,4567/tcp+udp,4568 on all three nodes","Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on each node with correct per-node wsrep_node_address/name and fixed wsrep_provider path to /usr/lib64/galera/libgalera_smm.so","Set SELinux boolean daemons_enable_cluster_mode=on persistently on all three nodes to fix a mariadb-backup SST connectto denial","Bootstrapped Galera on node1 via galera_new_cluster, set root password, created sstuser and appuser, created appdb.orders with 3 seed rows","Joined node2 and node3 to the cluster via mariabackup SST; verified wsrep_cluster_size=3 and full data replication on all nodes","Enabled mariadb.service for boot-time start on all three nodes","Inserted an additional pre-maintenance committed row (order-4) and confirmed it replicated to all nodes","Performed the maintenance-window shutdown: stopped mariadb on node3, then node2, then node1 (cluster fully down)","Identified node1 as the highest-seqno node (grastate.dat safe_to_bootstrap:1) and re-bootstrapped it, confirming all 4 rows present","Started node2 and node3, confirmed rejoin and a healthy 3/3 Synced/Primary cluster with all 4 rows present on every node","Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline on all three nodes plus healthy cluster/data proof","Rebooted node1, node2, then node3 one at a time via `reboot`, polling each until reachable again","Verified changed boot_id on each node after its reboot, and verified mariadb auto-started with wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary, and all 4 rows intact after each individual node's restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"3-member Galera cluster established across node1/node2/node3","command_ids":["cmd-ecce477f